WEBVTT

00:15.720 --> 00:18.560
I never dreamed before

00:18.560 --> 00:21.400
I'm gonna knock the door

00:21.400 --> 00:24.970
into the world of perfect free

00:24.970 --> 00:27.070
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:27.070 --> 00:29.910
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:29.910 --> 00:32.640
I'm gonna get the chance

00:32.640 --> 00:36.210
I thought a chance is far from me

00:36.210 --> 00:37.380
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:37.380 --> 00:40.280
I was made to hit in America

00:40.280 --> 00:43.150
(I was made to hit in America)

00:43.150 --> 00:49.060
I was made to hit in America

00:49.060 --> 00:52.730
You are the sun, you are the star

00:52.730 --> 00:54.730
(To me, forever)

00:54.730 --> 00:58.430
You are the sun, you are the star

00:58.430 --> 01:01.660
(To me, forever)

01:08.510 --> 01:14.120
I was made to hit in America

01:14.120 --> 01:16.950
I was made to hit in America

01:16.950 --> 01:19.820
(I was made to hit in America)

01:19.820 --> 01:22.620
I was made to hit in America

01:22.620 --> 01:25.390
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.390 --> 01:33.270
I was made to hit in America

02:16.950 --> 02:21.450
Gosh, it's noisy...
Oh no, it's started!

02:21.450 --> 02:22.780
Hey, you!

02:23.620 --> 02:27.250
Yikes! I guess we can't
ride the gondola.

02:28.690 --> 02:31.960
They've still got
the band member's story telling.

02:44.070 --> 02:46.130
Hey, it's the kid.

02:47.180 --> 02:48.240
Rikiya-kun!

02:48.240 --> 02:51.910
Didn't think I'd ever see you
standing on that stage.

02:51.910 --> 02:55.250
I didn't expect to see you, either.

02:55.250 --> 02:59.920
I'll be there watching you.
Give it your best shot!

02:59.920 --> 03:01.760
Thank you.

03:01.760 --> 03:04.760
Oh, and give my regards
to Ryusuke-kun too.

03:04.760 --> 03:06.250
How 'bout Chiba-kun?

03:07.260 --> 03:09.600
Hmph!

03:09.600 --> 03:12.090
-That wasn't good.
-Yeah...

03:15.800 --> 03:17.270
Oh, there you are!

03:17.650 --> 03:19.650
Hey! Koyuki!

03:19.650 --> 03:21.820
Maho! When did you get here?

03:21.820 --> 03:24.990
A little while ago.
The grounds are huge!

03:24.990 --> 03:26.320
Yeah, it's quite big.

03:26.320 --> 03:30.660
We'll be performing here...
This stage in the back.

03:30.660 --> 03:33.160
There're three big stages.

03:33.160 --> 03:35.330
Looks like there're
several smaller ones too.

03:35.330 --> 03:36.330
Uh-huh.

03:36.330 --> 03:39.100
Each band plays on each stage
at the same time.

03:39.100 --> 03:41.770
Hmm. Won't the sound be mixed up?

03:41.770 --> 03:45.110
Aw, I wanna see
Husking Bee from 3 PM.

03:45.110 --> 03:48.610
The stages are far from each other
so it won't be mixed up.

03:48.610 --> 03:50.280
There are trees too.

03:50.280 --> 03:52.950
Wow, Oil Octopus is going to play...

03:52.950 --> 03:56.620
-We're going to be on the 3rd stage, at 6:00.
-Wow, Apple will be playing too!

03:56.620 --> 03:57.960
Yeah.

03:57.960 --> 04:01.230
Hey, BECK and Yoshito
are playing at the same time!

04:01.230 --> 04:02.460
Really?!

04:02.460 --> 04:04.960
These two stages are far from each other,

04:04.960 --> 04:07.130
so we can only see one stage.

04:07.130 --> 04:09.300
I would take Yoshito on the main stage.

04:09.300 --> 04:10.700
He's my classmate.

04:11.130 --> 04:13.970
I'm dying to see Malcolm
on the second stage!

04:13.970 --> 04:16.960
-Um, Ryusuke-kun...
-Ryusuke?!

04:18.980 --> 04:21.480
Um, I'd rather not hear about him.

04:21.480 --> 04:22.980
Huh? Is something wrong?

04:22.980 --> 04:27.150
He's been really edgy
since last week...

04:27.150 --> 04:29.640
I haven't seen him since
we argued over the phone.

04:30.950 --> 04:35.660
-Maho, which...
-Koyuki! Good luck!

04:35.660 --> 04:37.630
Actually, we'll be...

04:39.430 --> 04:40.600
Hello?

04:40.600 --> 04:42.060
Ah, Yoshito!

04:43.600 --> 04:46.600
Really? You're staying
at the suite room?

04:46.600 --> 04:48.610
Yeah, we're coming!

04:48.610 --> 04:50.940
See ya, Koyuki-kun!

04:50.940 --> 04:52.280
Yeah.

04:52.280 --> 04:55.610
I wonder which stage
Maho-chan's coming to see.

04:55.610 --> 04:56.780
Hmm.

04:56.780 --> 04:59.180
Ooh, it's cold!

04:59.180 --> 05:01.880
This could stop your heart! Serious!

05:07.290 --> 05:09.990
They're counting the
number of people there.

05:10.790 --> 05:16.630
There is no way we could get a bigger
audience than Eiji's band or Malcolm!

05:16.630 --> 05:18.970
Yeah, the facilities are different too.

05:19.970 --> 05:22.970
That deal you made
with Leon is outrageous!

05:22.970 --> 05:27.980
If we lose this bet, the only
option left is for us to disband.

05:27.980 --> 05:30.640
I wonder if there are any good ideas.

05:31.820 --> 05:34.650
I still believe in the possibility.

05:34.650 --> 05:38.760
What is it with this
"possibility" of yours?

05:38.760 --> 05:40.310
You mean Koyuki's song?

05:41.490 --> 05:42.090
It's the dream.

05:42.090 --> 05:44.080
-Uh...Dream?
-Eek!

05:44.930 --> 05:46.400
That dream we all saw.

05:47.930 --> 05:51.260
That was definitely an omen.

05:53.940 --> 05:58.440
A dream! You idiot!
I never saw such a dream!

05:58.440 --> 06:00.110
Chiba!

06:00.110 --> 06:01.600
-Chiba...
-Uh...

06:06.450 --> 06:11.620
Maybe you weren't meant
to be a part of this band.

06:19.460 --> 06:20.630
"Weren't meant to be
a part of this band?"

06:20.630 --> 06:22.620
What the hell
are you talking about?

06:24.300 --> 06:27.790
Every member is needed in BECK.

06:28.810 --> 06:32.810
Ryusuke, what we saw was just a dream.

06:32.810 --> 06:37.140
It's true this area is littered
'cause the people have no manners...

06:40.920 --> 06:45.920
It's okay, Taira-kun...
The guy who created BECK says so...

06:45.920 --> 06:47.360
So I'll...

06:47.360 --> 06:50.660
-Hey, Chiba! Chiba, wait!
-Dammit!

06:52.100 --> 06:56.770
It really bothered him that he was
the only one who didn't see that dream.

06:56.770 --> 06:58.670
Even the Beatles and the Stones...

06:58.670 --> 07:01.570
...changed their members
right before their debut.

07:01.570 --> 07:05.110
-Chiba cares about this band
more than anyone...
-This isn't a social club!

07:05.110 --> 07:07.270
We can't make it big like that!

07:11.450 --> 07:13.940
Do you really mean that?

07:15.620 --> 07:19.280
If Chiba quits BECK...
I'm quitting too!

07:22.290 --> 07:24.630
Maria seems like a
really aggressive girl.

07:24.630 --> 07:28.470
Oh, her...You better tell
Koyuki to be careful.

07:28.470 --> 07:29.300
Huh?

07:29.300 --> 07:31.960
Maria's a nymphomaniac!

07:38.410 --> 07:40.080
What! Chiba-kun left?!

07:40.080 --> 07:41.410
His whereabouts unknown?

07:41.410 --> 07:44.580
He's turned off his cell phone,
I can't contact him at all.

07:44.580 --> 07:46.750
What about our performance?

07:46.750 --> 07:48.490
Anyway, let's split up
and search for him.

07:48.490 --> 07:51.820
It's 3:00 now,
so we still have 3 hours.

07:51.820 --> 07:53.820
I'll go take a look
at the campsite.

07:53.820 --> 07:55.660
Then, I'll search the stages.

07:55.660 --> 07:57.990
I'll check out the gates.

08:12.440 --> 08:15.110
What a bubbly stage...

08:15.110 --> 08:18.950
My sister's vision of the
Grateful Sound is barely alive.

08:18.950 --> 08:21.120
Seems like there's more
posers than before.

08:21.120 --> 08:23.120
Yeah, but you get to see bands
you wouldn't ordinarily see...

08:23.120 --> 08:25.960
I think it's okay.

08:25.960 --> 08:27.520
Hey, I just saw her panties!

08:27.520 --> 08:29.290
Really?!

08:33.960 --> 08:35.130
I swear!

08:35.130 --> 08:36.790
"Please recycle even if
this station is unmanned."

08:35.130 --> 08:36.790
I swear!

08:40.070 --> 08:41.630
Chiba-kun!

08:43.240 --> 08:46.300
Chiba-kun's things...
Thank goodness.

08:47.580 --> 08:51.080
-Hi, Koyuki.
-Hmm? Maria?

08:51.080 --> 08:54.150
Hey, is it true that guys get high...

08:54.150 --> 08:57.250
...and wanna make love
before the live show starts?

08:57.250 --> 09:01.590
Uh? I don't have time to talk now...
I've got to find...

09:07.600 --> 09:10.930
Hey, Koyuki? What are you doing?

09:14.600 --> 09:17.270
N-no...It's not...Maho!

09:30.790 --> 09:32.280
Chiba-kun...

09:48.570 --> 09:50.810
Chiba-kun...

09:50.810 --> 09:53.640
Where are you, Chiba-kun!?

09:54.910 --> 09:57.980
Mr. Chiba of the Mongolian Chop Squad,

09:57.980 --> 10:00.920
your friends are waiting
for you at the 3rd stage.

10:00.920 --> 10:05.560
I repeat, Mr. Chiba of
the Mongolian Chop Squad...

10:05.560 --> 10:07.760
...your friends are waiting
for you at the 3rd stage.

10:07.760 --> 10:11.660
Maybe...you weren't meant
to be a part of this band.

10:21.270 --> 10:22.940
I'm sorry Taira-kun.

10:22.940 --> 10:25.670
Take care, Koyuki, Saku...

10:46.230 --> 10:50.430
Chiba-kun! I'm sorry,
I made a mistake.

10:54.740 --> 11:00.470
I was planning to go straight home,
but since these guys are here...

11:07.920 --> 11:14.150
Generation 69. If I hadn't met
this band, where would I be now?

11:24.270 --> 11:26.430
Didn't it get a bit chilly?

11:28.100 --> 11:31.270
You think? Wanna eat the pork?

11:31.270 --> 11:34.510
I wonder if BECK's performance
is going to be alright...

11:58.130 --> 12:01.830
She's amazing.
I'm completely her fan now.

12:02.140 --> 12:04.130
Yes, she's the real deal.

12:04.980 --> 12:08.380
But most of the troops are still at the
main stage, or if not, at the second stage...

12:08.380 --> 12:09.980
Can't beat those numbers.

12:09.980 --> 12:11.720
That's absolutely impossible.

12:11.720 --> 12:13.120
To garner more people
than the main stage,

12:13.120 --> 12:14.850
or even the second stage
for that matter.

12:14.850 --> 12:16.750
It would take a miracle.

12:21.320 --> 12:22.330
What's up?

12:22.330 --> 12:23.990
Let's give up.

12:23.990 --> 12:24.660
What?

12:24.660 --> 12:27.330
Eiji's band on the main stage
is booked solid.

12:27.330 --> 12:29.370
Even Malcolm on the second stage,

12:29.370 --> 12:32.340
who's sold over
20 million CDs in the US...

12:32.340 --> 12:36.000
There's no way a band like us on
the third stage can beat those numbers.

12:37.270 --> 12:41.000
And besides, without Chiba,
we can't perform live.

12:44.610 --> 12:46.780
We still have one more hour.

12:46.780 --> 12:49.950
We're searching for Chiba now.

12:49.950 --> 12:52.790
I saw you from the hotel.

12:52.790 --> 12:55.190
What are you doing here
before the stage?

12:56.960 --> 13:00.020
Hey Ryusuke, are you listening? Hey!

13:01.130 --> 13:04.300
You remember what happens
to the loser now, huh?

13:04.300 --> 13:07.600
Yeah, we're having problems
because of that.

13:07.600 --> 13:08.630
Hmph.

13:12.480 --> 13:13.810
You running away?

13:16.480 --> 13:19.150
Yup, I'm more of a pest than I look.

13:19.150 --> 13:22.310
Watch your back, kid.
He really hates you.

13:28.660 --> 13:29.820
Come with me.

13:31.330 --> 13:33.330
I have something for you.

13:33.330 --> 13:35.160
Alright, let's go!

13:40.270 --> 13:43.670
-Let me go! Let me go!
-Hold him down!

13:57.620 --> 13:59.350
Hey, it's cold!

14:06.960 --> 14:08.950
There's no more time left.

14:17.470 --> 14:18.810
Chiba-kun!?

14:28.150 --> 14:30.820
This guy has calmed down
all of a sudden.

14:30.820 --> 14:34.160
Yeah. Malcolm and Belle Ame
are about to start.

14:34.160 --> 14:35.820
Today's main events, huh?

14:35.990 --> 14:38.600
Untie me! I'm going home.

14:38.600 --> 14:39.650
Huh?

14:57.450 --> 15:02.050
If I can't sing from the heart,

15:02.050 --> 15:07.960
then what is this song for...

15:07.960 --> 15:12.660
You're still here, haven't disappeared,

15:12.660 --> 15:18.000
Still going on strong...

15:28.980 --> 15:32.580
Everybody! The ground's
wet and slippery,

15:32.580 --> 15:36.150
so don't push the folks
in front of you!

15:36.150 --> 15:38.920
Then, let me introduce him to you...

15:38.920 --> 15:40.990
Let's call him out here...

15:40.990 --> 15:42.660
All right, here we go...

15:42.660 --> 15:47.150
Yoshito Morozumi!

15:49.430 --> 15:53.770
Hi girls! Are you ready? Okay?!

15:53.770 --> 15:56.330
Morozumi!!

16:01.440 --> 16:06.280
Lying in the bed,
you said, "It's not happen..."

16:12.120 --> 16:14.450
Hey, what's security doing?

16:15.290 --> 16:18.490
We've had injuries
in past performances!

16:19.300 --> 16:21.300
17,000 at the main,

16:21.300 --> 16:23.970
10,200 at the second,

16:23.970 --> 16:26.800
500 at the third stage.

16:26.800 --> 16:30.310
Thanks, man. Keep me posted.

16:30.310 --> 16:31.930
That can't be a good match.

16:32.480 --> 16:36.310
Well, the rain surely fucked up
the equipment on the third stage...

16:36.310 --> 16:38.150
